# Quarkus GCS: automated tests

For Google Cloud Storage **get/put only**, tests use **`LocalStorageHelper`** (`com.google.cloud:google-cloud-nio`, test scope). That is an in-memory `Storage` backend. Do **not** call a real bucket. Do **not** Mockito / `@InjectMock` `Storage`. Do **not** start `fake-gcs-server` or Testcontainers for this.

Keep tests **single-threaded**. `LocalStorageHelper` is not thread-safe. If tests run in parallel, or you need signed URLs, generations, checksums, or IAM, stop using this helper.

Seed objects from **in-repo** files (`src/test/resources/...`). Do not read fixtures from GCS or a network share.

## Replace `Storage` in `@QuarkusTest`

Produce a test `Storage` from `LocalStorageHelper.getOptions().getService()`. `@Mock` so it replaces the Google client. Reset/seed in `@BeforeEach` (`getOptions()` resets the static fake).

```kotlin
@Mock
class TestStorageProducer {
    @Produces
    @Singleton
    fun storage(): Storage = LocalStorageHelper.getOptions().getService()
}

@QuarkusTest
class GcsGetPutTest {

    @Inject
    lateinit var storage: Storage

    @BeforeEach
    fun seedBucket() {
        LocalStorageHelper.getOptions()
        val bytes = javaClass.getResource("/gcs/hello.txt")!!.readBytes()
        storage.create(
            BlobInfo.newBuilder("test-bucket", "hello.txt").build(),
            bytes,
        )
    }

    @Test
    fun inboundApiReadsObject() {
        given()
            .get("/storage/hello")
            .then()
            .statusCode(200)
            .body(equalTo("hello\n"))
    }

    @Test
    fun inboundApiPutsNamedObject() {
        val objectName = "notes/${UUID.randomUUID()}.txt"
        val content = UUID.randomUUID().toString()

        given()
            .body(content)
            .post("/storage/$objectName")
            .then()
            .statusCode(201)

        assertObjectText("test-bucket", objectName, content)
    }

    private fun assertObjectText(bucket: String, objectName: String, content: String) {
        val blob = storage.get(bucket, objectName)
        assertNotNull(blob)
        assertEquals(objectName, blob.name)
        assertEquals(content, String(blob.getContent(), Charsets.UTF_8))
    }
}
```

Cover get and put through the **inbound HTTP API** (same as other controller tests). After a put, assert the object **name** and **text** via `assertObjectText(bucket, objectName, content)`. Do not stop at HTTP 201. Put tests must use a **UUID** object name and content so they do not depend on leftover objects or hardcoded strings.

Do not set `quarkus.google.cloud.storage.host-override` to a real emulator unless you have left this helper. Do not use production bucket names or credentials in test settings.
